# Core Standards

## Import paths

Always use the `@/*` path alias. Never use relative `../../` imports crossing module boundaries.

```typescript
// Correct
import connectDB from '@/lib/db/connect';
import { withAuth } from '@/lib/auth/guards';

// Wrong
import connectDB from '../../lib/db/connect';
```

The alias is defined in `tsconfig.json`: `"@/*": ["./src/*"]`.

## Zod validation — safeParse only

Never call `schema.parse(...)` in route handlers or anywhere that would leave a Zod error uncaught. Always use `safeParse` and return a structured error response:

```typescript
const validation = schema.safeParse(body);
if (!validation.success) {
  return validationErrorResponse(validation.error);
}
// safe to use validation.data
```

## API response helpers — always

Every value returned from an API route must go through a helper from `src/lib/api/response.ts`. Never use raw `NextResponse.json()` in route files.

```typescript
// Correct
return successResponse({ listing }, 201);
return errorResponse('Listing not found', 404);
return validationErrorResponse(zodError);
return handleError(error);

// Wrong
return NextResponse.json({ listing }, { status: 201 });
```

Available helpers: `successResponse`, `errorResponse`, `validationErrorResponse`, `unauthorizedResponse`, `forbiddenResponse`, `notFoundResponse`, `conflictResponse`, `serverErrorResponse`, `handleError`.

## Database calls — connectDB first

Every service function that executes a Mongoose query must call `await connectDB()` before any query. This is a no-op when already connected but required for cold serverless starts.

```typescript
export async function getListingById(id: string) {
  await connectDB(); // always first
  return Listing.findActiveById(id);
}
```

## Soft delete — never hard delete

Never call `.deleteOne()`, `.deleteMany()`, or `.findByIdAndDelete()` on production data. Always soft-delete:

```typescript
document.isDeleted = true;
document.deletedAt = new Date();
await document.save();
```

All queries must filter `{ isDeleted: false }` or use the static `findActive*` model helpers.

## No secrets in logs

Never log: passwords, JWT tokens, password reset tokens, email verification tokens, or phone numbers. The `logger` utility in `src/lib/config/env.ts` automatically strips output in production — use it instead of `console.log` directly in library code.

## Never auto-generate these files

AI must never create or modify:
- `package-lock.json`
- Any file in `.next/`
- Migration files (there are none — this project uses Mongoose, not Prisma)
- `.env.local`, `.env.production`, or any live environment file

